{
  "schema": 1,
  "written_by": "hand, from each probe's source text; acceptance from the open frontends' documented SVA support; never from yosys output",
  "method": "Each probe is one module holding exactly one assert, assume or cover. It is read by the built-in frontend (read_verilog -formal -sv) and by yosys-slang (read_slang), then prep -top m, then the formal cells ($assert $assume $cover $check $live $fair) are counted.",
  "invariant": "No silent drop: a frontend either refuses the probe with an ERROR, or accepts it and leaves exactly `cells` formal cells. An accepted probe with fewer cells is a silently dropped property and must surface as Did not run with reason dropped.",
  "acceptance_key": "accept or refuse, from the documented support of each frontend: the built-in frontend implements immediate assertions, initial assume and $initstate, but no concurrent property; yosys-slang implements immediate assertions and concurrent properties with a boolean body (disable iff, $past, $rose, $fell, $stable, $onehot0, ->), but no sequence, implication across cycles, named sequence or property, default clocking, initial assume or $initstate. null means the documented support does not settle the form, so only the invariant is asserted.",
  "class_key": "For refused temporal forms, the closed construct class a refusal maps to: implication, delay, repetition, sequence_op, named_sequence, default_clocking, liveness_op, other.",
  "probes": [
    { "probe": "matrix/01_imp_overlap", "construct": "a |-> b", "form": "temporal", "class": "implication", "cells": 1, "builtin": "refuse", "slang": "refuse" },
